@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+id: task-001-fix-lower-case-sku-lookup-free-shipping-threshold-line-vat-rounding
+type: task
+title: "Fix lower-case SKU lookup, free-shipping threshold, line VAT rounding"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## What was done
+
+Three reports, each a deviation from the README rules, each fixed with a test first:
+
+1. Lower-case SKU refused: `Catalog.find` only trimmed; it now uses `canonicalSku` (case-insensitive).
+2. Delivery charged at exactly €50.00: free shipping used `>`; the rule is "€50.00 or more", now `>=`.
+3. Line VAT one cent low (€1.99 at 22%: 0.4378 → 0.44): `lineVat` truncated; it now uses `percentOf`
+   (round half up), as the README states.
+
+Tests added in `test/catalog.test.ts` and `test/orders.test.ts`; `npm test` passes (19).
